254
00:20:52.668 --> 00:20:54.461
-Where'd you find it?
-Bet he stole it.

255
00:20:54.544 --> 00:20:56.672
[vagrant] "Stole it"? Come on.
Don't hurt my feelings.

256
00:20:56.755 --> 00:20:58.924
What do you take me for. huh?

257
00:20:59.007 --> 00:21:00.008
I found it.

258
00:21:00.092 --> 00:21:02.678
You did? Do you remember where?

259
00:21:02.761 --> 00:21:05.597
Well. why do I have to tell you guys
anything at all?

260
00:21:05.681 --> 00:21:08.267
Don't you know it's a crime
to sell someone else's phone?

261
00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:10.936
-Should I report this guy?
-[chuckles]

262
00:21:11.019 --> 00:21:11.853
Yeah. report it.

263
00:21:11.937 --> 00:21:16.108
Tell the police how three grown men
are harassing one innocent homeless guy.

264
00:21:16.191 --> 00:21:17.109
I should call too.

265
00:21:17.693 --> 00:21:19.236
Let's just punch this guy till he talks.

266
00:21:19.319 --> 00:21:20.779
-Easy.
-That's not a bad idea.

267
00:21:20.862 --> 00:21:22.531
but people are already looking at us.

268
00:21:22.614 --> 00:21:24.741
Well. there's an alley over there.
You guys wait here.

269
00:21:24.825 --> 00:21:26.576
I'll make this quick. okay?

270
00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:27.911
-All right. let's go.
-[stammers]

271
00:21:27.995 --> 00:21:29.830
-Move fast.
-Okay. someone threw it away.

272
00:21:30.414 --> 00:21:33.166
I saw a man put it in the trash.
so I took it.

273
00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:35.168
Please tell me you saw their face.

274
00:21:57.691 --> 00:21:59.276
This looks expensive.

275
00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:03.363
Hey. sir.

276
00:22:03.447 --> 00:22:04.531
Ta-da.

277
00:22:05.157 --> 00:22:06.241
Wanna make a trade?

278
00:22:11.538 --> 00:22:13.040
I'm not a criminal. okay?

279
00:22:13.123 --> 00:22:15.917
After I scored the soju.
I don't know what happened.

280
00:22:16.001 --> 00:22:17.336
Think hard. sir.

281
00:22:18.086 --> 00:22:20.380
The car color.
Or the license plate number.

282
00:22:20.464 --> 00:22:22.174
Do you remember anything?

283
00:22:22.257 --> 00:22:23.717
What about what they looked like?

284
00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:24.801
How many were there?

285
00:22:24.885 --> 00:22:27.304
How the hell could anyone know?

286
00:22:32.059 --> 00:22:34.644
Sir. I'm begging you. Try to remember.

287
00:22:36.063 --> 00:22:37.189
Please give me something.

288
00:22:40.067 --> 00:22:44.946
Well. the car was a white BMV.

289
00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:46.615
I'm not sure the plate number though.

290
00:22:46.698 --> 00:22:47.741
When was this?

291
00:22:48.784 --> 00:22:49.868
The middle of the night.

292
00:22:49.951 --> 00:22:51.119
I don't know what time.

293
00:22:51.703 --> 00:22:52.621
Uhâ€¦

294
00:22:52.704 --> 00:22:54.372
<i>He had a ponytail.</i>

295
00:22:54.456 --> 00:22:56.458
I-I promise that's all I know.

296
00:23:00.629 --> 00:23:01.838
[reporter]<i> In Myeongpo Port today.</i>

297
00:23:01.922 --> 00:23:04.758
<i>the forecast calls for mostly clear skies</i>
<i>during the day</i>

298
00:23:04.841 --> 00:23:06.676
<i>with a storm coming in at night.</i>

299
00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.262
<i>The localized downpour</i>
<i>is expected to be accompanied</i>

300
00:23:09.346 --> 00:23:12.933
<i>by thunder and lightning late tonight.</i>
<i>so caution is advised.</i>

301
00:23:16.061 --> 00:23:17.062
Hello. boss.

302
00:23:17.145 --> 00:23:18.396
Hey. rookie.

303
00:23:19.272 --> 00:23:21.399
Actually found a good warehouse for once.

304
00:23:21.483 --> 00:23:22.734
-Thank you. sir.
-So this is it?

305
00:23:22.818 --> 00:23:24.027
Did you eat dinner?

306
00:23:24.111 --> 00:23:25.403
Yeah. I just ate. sir.

307
00:23:26.196 --> 00:23:28.115
Gang-min. have we had dinner yet?

308
00:23:28.198 --> 00:23:30.826
No. sir. We haven't had anything all day.

309
00:23:30.909 --> 00:23:34.704
Right. but the rookie went ahead
and had dinner already.

310
00:23:34.788 --> 00:23:37.457
It's disrespectful to eat
before your elders. you know.

311
00:23:38.083 --> 00:23:39.084
I'm sorry. boss.

312
00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:41.962
[laughs] I'm just kidding.

313
00:23:42.796 --> 00:23:43.797
So what'd you eat?

314
00:23:44.297 --> 00:23:46.299
Well. I had sundae gukbap. sir.

315
00:23:46.383 --> 00:23:47.509
Spicy or what?

316
00:23:48.009 --> 00:23:49.970
No. but it was still really good.

317
00:23:50.053 --> 00:23:52.097
Well. you should cool down anyway!

318
00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:53.640
-[laughing]
-[water splashing]

319
00:23:53.723 --> 00:23:54.724
[rookie coughing]

320
00:23:54.808 --> 00:23:57.269
Get your ass out of there
once you've cooled down.

321
00:23:57.352 --> 00:23:58.895
-We don't have time to mess around.
-[rookie] I can't swim!

322
00:23:58.979 --> 00:24:00.981
-Should we move the body now?
-[Gang-min laughs]

323
00:24:01.064 --> 00:24:03.066
Let's eat first. It's not going anywhere.

324
00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:04.234
[chuckles]

325
00:24:04.317 --> 00:24:05.694
Sounds good to me.

326
00:24:16.079 --> 00:24:18.957
We don't know have a lot of info.
so let's just start with the car.

327
00:24:19.040 --> 00:24:19.875
Okay.

328
00:24:20.458 --> 00:24:22.627
White BMVâ€¦

329
00:24:35.724 --> 00:24:37.601
-Wait. is that him?
-[Jin-cheol] You found the driver?

330
00:24:37.684 --> 00:24:39.186
-Can you see his face?
-Let me zoom.

331
00:24:48.570 --> 00:24:49.654
Loading now.

332
00:24:50.822 --> 00:24:54.451
Kim Sang-man. 41 years old.
He has eight prior convictions.

333
00:24:54.534 --> 00:24:56.411
[Jin-cheol] Really? Eight priors for what?

334
00:24:56.494 --> 00:24:58.914
I bet they're all assault.
He sounds like an animal.

335
00:24:58.997 --> 00:24:59.998
Wait a minute.

336
00:25:01.249 --> 00:25:03.710
He got out of the back seat
so he wasn't alone.

337
00:25:03.793 --> 00:25:04.753
Good catch.

338
00:25:06.171 --> 00:25:08.173
So with all of the vehicle's details.

339
00:25:08.256 --> 00:25:10.717
I can plug them in here
and find its location.

340
00:25:12.010 --> 00:25:12.886
Hold on.

341
00:25:14.262 --> 00:25:16.389
SEARCHINGâ€¦

342
00:25:16.473 --> 00:25:19.726
Searching. It's in real time
so it can take a while.

343
00:25:19.809 --> 00:25:22.020
-[sighs]
-[Jin-cheol] How dare they kidnap Min-ji?

344
00:25:22.103 --> 00:25:24.731
I'll make 'em pay. Kim Sang-man.

345
00:25:26.983 --> 00:25:28.610
[groaning]

346
00:25:29.611 --> 00:25:30.487
The hell?

347
00:25:31.821 --> 00:25:32.948
You're trying to kill me?

348
00:25:34.699 --> 00:25:38.078
Body's been secured
and the location's been set.

349
00:25:38.161 --> 00:25:40.497
Now we just need to tie this
to Ju Gang-chan

350
00:25:40.580 --> 00:25:41.831
and we'll be good to go.

351
00:25:45.502 --> 00:25:47.420
[sighs] "Hey. Gang-chan.

352
00:25:48.672 --> 00:25:50.215
They say your daughterâ€¦

353
00:25:51.007 --> 00:25:53.009
killed someone on accident."

354
00:25:53.093 --> 00:25:56.513
[laughing]

355
00:25:59.766 --> 00:26:01.268
[laughing]

356
00:26:04.771 --> 00:26:08.525
Hey. sir. I still don't understand
why you're so obsessed with him. boss.

357
00:26:09.401 --> 00:26:12.445
Well. the question is.
how badly was he screwed over?

358
00:26:12.529 --> 00:26:15.740
[laughs] Here boss.
The biggest potato goes to you.

359
00:26:20.203 --> 00:26:21.121
[breathes shakily]

360
00:26:31.006 --> 00:26:32.215
Whoa. whoa. whoa!

361
00:26:33.425 --> 00:26:34.926
I'm sorry. sir! I'm sorry!

362
00:26:35.010 --> 00:26:37.679
[grunting]

363
00:26:40.515 --> 00:26:42.142
Please. sir. I'm sorry!

364
00:26:42.225 --> 00:26:43.560
[grunting]

365
00:26:50.442 --> 00:26:52.027
{\an8}9 YEARS AGO

366
00:26:52.110 --> 00:26:54.279
{\an8}-[clamoring]
-[protestor] Go away! Get out of here!

367
00:26:56.698 --> 00:26:59.409
Come on. I'll take on all of you! [grunts]

368
00:26:59.492 --> 00:27:00.744
STOP RECONSTRUCTION
THAT DESTROYS CITIZENS' LIVES

369
00:27:00.827 --> 00:27:03.163
Do you know how old
these apartment buildings are?

370
00:27:03.246 --> 00:27:04.414
I'm not sure. boss.

371
00:27:04.497 --> 00:27:06.041
They were built 40 years ago.

372
00:27:06.124 --> 00:27:08.585
And yet they still
won't approve the redevelopment.

373
00:27:08.668 --> 00:27:10.670
We need that approval so you and I
can get the money

374
00:27:10.754 --> 00:27:12.797
that we're owed for our services.

375
00:27:12.881 --> 00:27:14.049
[chuckles]

376
00:27:14.132 --> 00:27:15.008
You're right. sir.

377
00:27:15.091 --> 00:27:19.346
I wonder how many of these
still don't have a parking garage.

378
00:27:25.894 --> 00:27:27.395
[exclaims]

379
00:27:27.479 --> 00:27:28.772
-[crashes]
-[car alarm blaring]

380
00:27:36.988 --> 00:27:38.948
[reporter] <i>Behind me is the site</i>
<i>where a cleaner fell</i>

381
00:27:39.032 --> 00:27:40.950
<i>from a balcony at Midu Apartments.</i>

382
00:27:41.034 --> 00:27:42.994
{\an8}<i>After being transported to the hospital.</i>

383
00:27:43.078 --> 00:27:44.621
{\an8}the victim was taken into surgery

384
00:27:44.704 --> 00:27:47.290
{\an8}and remains unresponsive.
still in critical care.

385
00:27:47.374 --> 00:27:49.459
{\an8}The owner of the building
has declined to comment.

386
00:27:49.542 --> 00:27:52.212
{\an8}Residents have been voicing their concerns
as they complain

387
00:27:52.295 --> 00:27:55.090
<i>that the dangerously low railing</i>
<i>makes the walkway unsafe.</i>

388
00:27:55.173 --> 00:27:58.009
<i>Also. cracks across the exterior walls</i>
<i>have been found.</i>

389
00:27:58.093 --> 00:28:02.180
<i>so residents claim that repair work alone</i>
<i>can no longer hold the building together.</i>

390
00:28:03.848 --> 00:28:05.934
<i>After failing to pass review for years.</i>

391
00:28:06.017 --> 00:28:09.270
<i>the redevelopment of Midu Apartments</i>
<i>has finally been green lit.</i>

392
00:28:09.354 --> 00:28:11.689
<i>The announcement of the approval</i>
<i>was given by the government</i>

393
00:28:11.773 --> 00:28:12.690
<i>on the 19th.</i>

394
00:28:12.774 --> 00:28:15.819
<i>who also issued a maintenance plan</i>
<i>to continue to keep it safe.</i>

395
00:28:16.444 --> 00:28:19.197
<i>Experts say this approval</i>
<i>for the redevelopment of the apartmentsâ€¦</i>

396
00:28:19.280 --> 00:28:20.740
[groaning]

397
00:28:24.411 --> 00:28:26.913
Look. man.
I was just doing what I was told.

398
00:28:26.996 --> 00:28:29.165
Jung-dae. you have to believe me.

399
00:28:29.249 --> 00:28:30.917
-I swear Iâ€¦ [groans]
-[grunts]

400
00:28:32.377 --> 00:28:33.920
[groans]

401
00:28:36.214 --> 00:28:38.716
[Jung-dae]
This isn't how I wanted to go freelance.

402
00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:39.634
{\an8}CEO YANG SEOK-CHEOL

403
00:28:41.803 --> 00:28:43.221
Ah. shit.

404
00:28:43.304 --> 00:28:46.057
Who knew that it would be so easy
to take the throne?

405
00:28:46.975 --> 00:28:48.393
I should've done this sooner.

406
00:28:50.645 --> 00:28:52.188
[people cheering]

407
00:28:54.983 --> 00:28:56.568
Trust in me alone.

408
00:28:57.235 --> 00:28:58.194
Don't cross me.

409
00:28:58.278 --> 00:28:59.821
Here's to our success.

410
00:29:00.780 --> 00:29:01.990
To us.

411
00:29:02.073 --> 00:29:04.117
[cheering]

412
00:29:06.327 --> 00:29:08.538
-[Jung-dae] Tell the girls to come.
-[underling] Yes. sir.

413
00:29:08.621 --> 00:29:09.706
[cheering]

414
00:29:09.789 --> 00:29:11.291
-Boss. you got a call.
-[phone buzzing]

415
00:29:12.125 --> 00:29:13.418
Hey. [shushes]

416
00:29:14.252 --> 00:29:15.253
Who's this?

417
00:29:15.336 --> 00:29:17.005
[Nam] <i>This is Juhak Construction.</i>

418
00:29:17.672 --> 00:29:19.382
<i>The chairman would like to meet with you.</i>

419
00:29:31.644 --> 00:29:33.772
Heard there's been a change in management.

420
00:29:34.439 --> 00:29:36.316
You used to work for Mr. Yang. right?

421
00:29:37.317 --> 00:29:39.277
[sighs] Listen. young man.

422
00:29:39.360 --> 00:29:40.445
I know who you are.

423
00:29:41.154 --> 00:29:44.157
I know what you can do.
You're gonna be useful to me.

424
00:29:44.991 --> 00:29:48.995
[sighs]
You know. I forgot you even existed.

425
00:29:49.871 --> 00:29:51.623
It was you. right? [blows]

426
00:29:52.540 --> 00:29:55.794
You were the coward
who gave the order to Yang. weren't you?

427
00:29:56.503 --> 00:29:57.629
Stand down.

428
00:29:59.964 --> 00:30:01.841
I believe there's a misunderstanding.

429
00:30:02.342 --> 00:30:03.676
I never gave him that order.

430
00:30:04.969 --> 00:30:08.306
All I said was that I wish someone
would just jump off and die there.

431
00:30:08.389 --> 00:30:09.599
-That's all.
-What?

432
00:30:09.682 --> 00:30:11.851
[chuckles] Geez.

433
00:30:13.770 --> 00:30:16.397
Yang was seriously incompetent. wasn't he?

434
00:30:18.233 --> 00:30:19.859
He couldn't even kill you.

435
00:30:24.697 --> 00:30:25.824
Show no mercy.

436
00:30:29.828 --> 00:30:32.038
[exclaiming]

437
00:30:37.877 --> 00:30:39.170
Die. motherfucker!

438
00:30:39.254 --> 00:30:40.505
[grunts]

439
00:30:41.714 --> 00:30:43.633
[choking]

440
00:30:53.852 --> 00:30:56.271
[shouting. grunting]

441
00:30:59.816 --> 00:31:02.068
[grunting]

442
00:31:03.403 --> 00:31:04.529
[groans]

443
00:31:08.116 --> 00:31:10.076
[grunting]

444
00:31:13.121 --> 00:31:14.372
[groans]

445
00:31:21.796 --> 00:31:23.506
[grunts. groans]

446
00:31:33.850 --> 00:31:35.393
[grunts]

447
00:31:55.705 --> 00:31:59.125
When I was a kid.
my next-door neighbor had a huge dog.

448
00:32:04.756 --> 00:32:08.551
Unfortunately it was feral
and bit the owner one too many times.

449
00:32:08.635 --> 00:32:12.347
Eventually. the owner snapped
and tried to beat the poor dog to death.

450
00:32:14.307 --> 00:32:16.935
But I managed to persuade them
to give it to me.

451
00:32:19.228 --> 00:32:21.689
I actually liked the dog.
because it was feral.

452
00:32:24.108 --> 00:32:26.694
[fire crackling. sizzling]

453
00:32:31.240 --> 00:32:33.660
Do you know how
I was able to tame that dog?

454
00:32:38.623 --> 00:32:41.584
I made sure it could never
bite its owner again.

455
00:32:50.093 --> 00:32:53.429
[ominous music playing]

456
00:33:04.232 --> 00:33:05.942
[groans]

457
00:33:07.193 --> 00:33:09.529
-[tool clicking]
-[Jung-dae groaning]

458
00:33:19.622 --> 00:33:20.748
[Jung-dae gasps]

459
00:33:21.374 --> 00:33:22.792
[whimpers]

460
00:33:22.875 --> 00:33:24.293
Say. "Ah."

461
00:33:26.796 --> 00:33:30.174
[grunting. groaning]

462
00:33:33.344 --> 00:33:36.431
[shouting]

463
00:33:39.267 --> 00:33:41.477
So do you feel like being a good boy now?

464
00:33:42.395 --> 00:33:44.397
I could pour boiling water
down your throat.

465
00:33:44.480 --> 00:33:46.524
then you really
won't be able to bark again.

466
00:33:47.900 --> 00:33:49.819
[groaning]

467
00:33:56.534 --> 00:33:58.202
I'll do anything.

468
00:33:58.286 --> 00:34:01.330
[breathes shakily]
Please. I'll be your dog.

469
00:34:01.414 --> 00:34:04.751
I'll do whatever you say. sir.
Whatever you want.

470
00:34:04.834 --> 00:34:07.837
[crying] Just please let me live.

471
00:34:09.589 --> 00:34:11.632
[crying]

472
00:34:19.599 --> 00:34:21.142
It'll be dark soon.

473
00:34:21.225 --> 00:34:23.436
Let's tidy up
and get ready to move the body.

474
00:34:23.519 --> 00:34:25.021
-Okay. [groans]
-Yes. sir.

475
00:34:26.397 --> 00:34:28.566
-[Gang-min groans]
-[cutlery clatters]

476
00:34:32.737 --> 00:34:34.947
[tense music playing]

477
00:34:44.707 --> 00:34:48.753
Oh. geez. can you stop being so butthurt
about a couple of punches?

478
00:34:49.796 --> 00:34:51.464
Want me to call your mom?

479
00:34:51.547 --> 00:34:52.965
No. I'm perfectly fine. sir!

480
00:34:56.844 --> 00:34:57.970
Boss. we're here now!

481
00:34:58.054 --> 00:35:00.890
-[Jung-dae] Yeah. I have eyes. you idiot!
-[Gang-min] Of course. sir!

482
00:35:14.946 --> 00:35:16.656
[grunts]

483
00:35:28.835 --> 00:35:31.379
Damn. I forgot how heavy dead bodies are.

484
00:35:31.462 --> 00:35:32.505
Stop whining.

485
00:35:38.636 --> 00:35:39.637
[guard] Hey. freeze!

486
00:35:40.638 --> 00:35:42.014
What are you doing here?

487
00:35:46.602 --> 00:35:47.436
What is that?

488
00:35:48.229 --> 00:35:49.939
[inhales deeply]

489
00:35:50.022 --> 00:35:51.816
-It's a dead girl.
-What?

490
00:35:52.483 --> 00:35:53.568
A dead girl?

491
00:35:53.651 --> 00:35:54.694
[sighs]

492
00:35:54.777 --> 00:35:57.989
At your age. you should already be
in bed by now. Jesus.

493
00:35:58.072 --> 00:35:59.407
Sang-man. go.

494
00:35:59.490 --> 00:36:00.491
Yes. sir.

495
00:36:02.243 --> 00:36:03.286
[both groan]

496
00:36:03.911 --> 00:36:05.663
It's not what you think. sir.

497
00:36:05.746 --> 00:36:07.707
We rented this freezer warehouse to. uhâ€¦

498
00:36:07.790 --> 00:36:09.667
I'll just show you the contract.

499
00:36:10.418 --> 00:36:11.586
Where is it?

500
00:36:11.669 --> 00:36:13.379
[ominous music plays]

501
00:36:13.462 --> 00:36:14.547
[guard] What are you doing?

502
00:36:19.510 --> 00:36:21.554
It's still not done yet?
How much longer now?

503
00:36:23.347 --> 00:36:25.183
